# Commit after each phase

When a phase in a technical PRD (`ai-workspace/*_prd.md`) is complete — its tests pass, its acceptance criteria are checked, and its status marker is updated — stop there.

Remind the user to commit before the next phase starts. Do not create the commit unless they ask. Do not start the next phase in the same turn.

Say what would be committed, in one or two sentences, and suggest a commit message that says why the phase exists. Example:

> Phase 1 is done. Commit `migrations/0002_create-mcq.sql` and `migrations/create-mcq.test.ts` before Phase 2?
>
> Suggested message: `Add the questions, choices, and attempts tables.`

If the user asks to start the next phase while the finished phase is still uncommitted, remind them once and ask whether to commit first or continue.
